  "subject": "Development Project 4 target-aware project compilation",
  "claim": "The maintained focused Project 4 selection passes 14 cases on Windows and real Debian with retained native products. The existing Option/Result text-borrow consumer compiles through native project parsing, source admission, authentication, analysis, and emission. Source reordering yields identical WVB bytes. Existing-output preservation, missing/duplicate/escaping target, Project 3 rejection, missing target/profile files, malformed/oversized/hardlinked target, wrong lock digest, and target/platform mismatch reject without publication. All 13 existing coordinator failure/cleanup sentinel groups also pass on both hosts.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "Other",
    "value": "Base c0be29f4 plus the exact current-source inputs recorded below. The package migration is excluded: this maintained selection uses the committed Foundation text-borrow fixture and Option/Result libraries. Retained producer labels resolve by exact byte size and SHA-256, not a machine-specific cache path."
